  "history": {
    "originCountries": [
      "Spain"
    ],
    "origins": "Tute originated in Italy as tutti and spread to Spain in the 19th century, becoming one of the most popular card games there. Tute gana-pierde is a Spanish variant in which the player with the most points loses unless someone reaches 101 or more to win; it is played by three to five players individually.",
    "timeline": [
      "19th century: Tute spread to Spain; gana-pierde (win-lose) variant emerged with target 101 and most-points-loses rule."
